WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.654
Team energy is a shared operating constraint.

00:00:02.654 --> 00:00:07.033
A group can have enough people and still lack the collective capacity

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:10.317
for good execution if communication load is too high,

00:00:10.317 --> 00:00:14.331
ownership is unclear, meetings are excessive, or interruption culture prevents focus.

00:00:14.331 --> 00:00:17.980
Team performance is not only a sum of individual motivation.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.359
It is shaped by the system that distributes attention, decisions, and recovery.

00:00:22.359 --> 00:00:24.183
Communication load deserves careful design.

00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:26.737
Too little communication creates confusion and rework.

00:00:26.737 --> 00:00:29.656
Too much communication creates noise and constant checking.

00:00:29.656 --> 00:00:34.035
Clear ownership reduces energy drain because people know who decides, who contributes,

00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:37.684
who needs to be informed, and where escalation should go.

00:00:37.684 --> 00:00:42.428
Escalation paths matter because unresolved uncertainty can consume attention across an entire team.

00:00:42.428 --> 00:00:47.171
Psychological safety at a practical level means people can raise risks, ask questions,

00:00:47.171 --> 00:00:50.820
admit uncertainty, and challenge assumptions without unnecessary punishment or humiliation.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.280
This is not softness.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.104
It is a reliability mechanism.

00:00:54.104 --> 00:00:58.483
Teams waste less energy hiding problems when they can discuss them early.

00:00:58.483 --> 00:01:03.957
They also make better decisions when people can surface constraints before those constraints become failures.

00:01:03.957 --> 00:01:06.876
Sustainable pace reduces reliance on heroic individual effort.

00:01:06.876 --> 00:01:09.795
Heroics may be necessary during a real incident,

00:01:09.795 --> 00:01:13.079
but they should not become the standard operating model.

00:01:13.079 --> 00:01:15.998
Protecting focus time, respecting recovery and non-work commitments,

00:01:15.998 --> 00:01:20.742
reducing unnecessary meetings, and clarifying priorities all help teams use energy more wisely.

00:01:20.742 --> 00:01:26.580
A team that treats energy as shared capacity can execute more reliably without burning people down.
